s-to-milestone'.\\n\\nIMPORTANT FINDING: `/groom-milestone` does not exist anywhere in the codebase. The description's claim that `/groom-milestone` is the correct replacement is unverified and appears incorrect. Before making any change, the implementer must verify:\\n1. Whether `/start-milestone` is accessible to users of this skill (both are project-level skills in `.claude/skills/`)\\n2. Whether the concern is that `group-items-to-milestone` will be moved to the plugin and would then need a different reference\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Run `grep -n 'start-milestone' .claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 confirm line 113 contains `Next step: /start-milestone {number}`\\n2. Confirm `/start-milestone` skill exists: `ls .claude/skills/start-milestone/SKILL.md` exits 0\\n3. Confirm `/groom-milestone` does NOT exist: `find . -name 'SKILL.md' | xargs grep -l 'name: groom-milestone' 2>/dev/null` returns empty\\n4. If the fix is to update the reference: run `grep -n 'start-milestone' .claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md` again and confirm the line is changed to the correct skill name\\n5. Run `uv run prek run --files .claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 exits 0 with no lint errors\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- `/groom-milestone` does not exist anywhere in the codebase. The description says the correct next step is `/groom-milestone` but this appears incorrect. Is the intent to CREATE a `/groom-milestone` skill, or should the existing `/start-milestone` reference be kept?\\n- If the concern is that `group-items-to-milestone` will be moved to the plugin while `start-milestone` remains project-level, the fix is a documentation note about the cross-namespace dependency \u2014 not a skill name change.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| File | `.claude/skills/group-items-to-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014 file to edit, line 113 |\\n| File | `.claude/skills/start-milestone/SKILL.md` \u2014